The attached image, Figure 6 from the npj Vaccines (2017) paper, demonstrates how Nano-11 enhances antigen targeting and retention. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs), potent antigen-presenting cells (APCs), exhibit the highest CD86 expression in the draining lymph node. Panel B further characterizes OVA-positive cells, indicating that most MigDCs containing antigen are CD11b+Ly6C-, an effective DC subtype. Panel C illustrates that soluble OVA rapidly clears from the injection site, but OVA adjuvanted with Nano-11 (or aluminum hydroxide) is retained for a significantly longer period (up to 7 days), thus prolonging antigen availability for immune activation.